window.products.push({"id":110913,"name":"Dryer Heating Element 279838 & Fuse 279816 Replacement Fits Whirlpool Kenmore Roper","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":48.5,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/715Wt9B+kPL._AC_SL1200_.jpg","description":"279838 Dryer Heating Heater Element Installation Notes Dryer heating element. If your dryer does not heat first check for a blown thermal fuse on the blower housing before replacing the heating element. In most cases the heating element will have a break in the element if defective. Dryer thermal fuse. Located on the blower housing. If the dryer overheats, the thermal fuse blows to cut off power to the dryer. If the thermal fuse has blown, the dryer won't start. The thermal fuse cannot be reset—if the fuse has blown, replace it. Thermal fuses often blow due to a clogged vent. 279816 dryer thermostat cut-off kit Installation Notes The thermal cut off turns off the heating component when the dryer overheats, ensuring there is a consistent level of heat at all times. This 279816 dryer thermostat cut-off kit includes one high-limit thermostat with a limit of 250 degrees Fahrenheit, and one thermal cut-off fuse (309 degrees). This kit also includes flat heaters with jumper wires. If your dryer is not starting properly, to be replaced. PART SPECIFICATIONS Dryer Element Kit Including 279838, 279816 -The element is rated at 5400 Watts 240 Volts and has 2- 5/16\" male terminals.-The Heater replaces part # 3403585 as well as other numbers.-The element is fully assembled in a housing for easy installation.-The Thermostat # 279816 includes 3 pieces:-Thermal Fuse #3977393 is 309*F.-Thermostat #3390291 is 250*F/122*C.-Jumper wire to be used when replacing 3 wire thermostat #3977767.-The 3390291 thermostat is included in 2 kits offered, the other kit is # 279769 & in that kit it includes a 352*F thermal fuse, when replacing both pieces at the same time, (it is importantto) replace a 309 w/ a 309 (279816) or a 352 w/ a 352 (279769). Fixes the following symptoms: No heat or not enough heat. Takes too long to dry. Will Not Start. Too hot. Shuts off too soon.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/715Wt9B+kPL._AC_SL1200_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"X clouds Electrical","source_asin":"B076GZBXYS","category_path":"Home & Appliances"},"sku":"BM-110913","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B076GZBXYS","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Appliances.jsonl","source_asin":"B076GZBXYS","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
